From f37d15570308edbaedc2f6b3e5bf3d7fd53a4066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] resume: deleted chats are terminal, not unfinished
 drafts (desktop-03cd4d73b3)

session.resume treated a missing row plus a surviving minted_session_keys
record as a never-persisted draft and tried to materialize it; the
transactional resurrection fence refused with RuntimeStoreError(not_found),
logged as a WARNING traceback, and the boot sweep kept the turn marker so it
retried every restart in the freshness window.

- methods_session: check the selected store's retirement fence before
  materializing a minted key; a retired id returns 4007 with
  data.reason=session_deleted and an INFO log. A delete racing the
  create (fence refuses with not_found) is the same terminal outcome,
  quiet. Other storage failures keep their warning.
- startup_resume: on session_deleted, retire the marker in its own
  profile home (clear_turn_marker) and log an INFO skip; a plain 4007
  or store error keeps the marker.
- tests: real temp-DB delete/retire cases, racing delete, named profile
  store, unexpected-failure and valid-draft controls.
